Before modifying individual implementation classes, make sure the common utility supports every API.

Your current methods are already extended with `Long responseTime`. Keep that design.

I recommend adding an additional generic helper for direct SendFlex calls, where you need to construct a DTO yourself:

```java
public SendFlexRecordDto saveSendFlexRecord(
        Object request,
        Object response,
        String apiCode,
        String statusCode,
        Long responseTime) {

    SendFlexRecordDto dto = SendFlexRecordDto.builder()
            .requestObject(request)
            .responseObject(response)
            .apiCode(apiCode)
            .statusCode(statusCode)
            .responseTime(responseTime)
            .build();

    return saveSendflexRecord(dto);
}
```

This allows APIs such as Address Validation and Metering to use the same persistence mechanism without duplicating DTO-building code.

For failures, you can pass the exception message as the response object, or retain your existing structured error-response handling.

